  "name": "IHC - CD-43",
  "code": "1876",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul class=\"marker:text-textOff list-disc\">\n<li>\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">CD43 expression is identified on T lymphocytes and myeloid lineage cells (including monocytes, granulocytes, and subsets of B lymphocytes).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">Positive staining for CD43 supports the identification of hematolymphoid cells, especially in the context of lymphomas or leukemia.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">In disease settings: CD43 is expressed in most T-cell lymphomas, a subset of B-cell lymphomas (especially CLL/SLL, mantle cell, Burkitt), and some myeloid neoplasms.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 11px;\">\n<p class=\"my-0\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px;\">The result should be interpreted with clinical, morphological, and flow cytometric findings</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
